{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHqcMcHFw8A5V7xyQh4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 18 (Sb fraction 0.664)** as the best composition. At 0.0327% it had the highest EQE of the five compositions I measured. That used the whole EQE budget; I spent none of the 5 XRD measurements.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 8 | 0.365 | 0.0132 |\n| 13 | 0.519 | 0.0156 |\n| 17 | 0.641 | 0.0306 |\n| **18** | **0.664** | **0.0327** |\n| 22 | 0.763 | 0.0238 |\n\n1. **Coarse scan:** I measured four points across the middle of the line. EQE rose with Sb content and peaked between Sb 0.52 and 0.76.\n2. **Last measurement:** the built-in Gaussian-process suggester recommended index 29. Its predictions didn't match the data (predicted means of about 0.007% against measured values up to 0.031%), so I didn't follow it. Instead I fitted a parabola through the three points around the peak. It put the maximum at Sb ≈ 0.66, and measuring that composition (index 18) gave the highest value.\n\nThe ends of the line are unmeasured: below Sb 0.37 (indices 0–7) and above Sb 0.76 (indices 23–29). EQE was falling toward both ends, so a second, better region there seems unlikely, but I can't rule it out. Index 18 is also only 7% above its neighbour at index 17. I didn't check the crystal phases with XRD, so the result rests on the EQE numbers alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":8339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":530,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65b3c2e2-01bb-4b48-b6d6-bb42756aef6d","uuid":"811674b0-b09d-4ff8-b02c-a932227716e9","timestamp":"2026-09-1